From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caomengxuan666 <2507560089@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:03:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(niu): re-target the Niu shell delta onto upstream
 ce0323f2f2

The fork was pinned to upstream 2230d64464 (2026-08-12) and had drifted 3180
commits. `sync-upstream.sh check` reported PATCH CONFLICT, and for good reason:
the delta could not be rebased, only re-implemented.

What upstream removed underneath the delta:

- `shell-command/src/command_safety/is_safe_command.rs` is gone, along with the
  `is_known_safe_command` / `is_safe_to_call_with_exec` allowlist. Shell wrappers
  such as `bash -lc "..."` are no longer "known safe" by name, so Niu needs no
  equivalent entry; the fork's `niu -C "git status"` test was dropped.
- `ToolUserShellType` and `tool_user_shell_type` are gone, so the fork's
  `Niu` arm and its enum variant were dropped too.
- `create_shell_command_tool`'s PowerShell description was replaced by
  `exec_command`, so the fork's description reword had no target. The surviving
  piece of that intent, the `<shell>niu</shell>` bullet in
  `windows_shell_guidance()`, is kept.
- `get_shell()` and the `get_*_shell()` helpers lost their `path` parameter, so
  `get_niu_shell()` was rewritten to the new signature.

What upstream added that now needs Niu arms: `capture_script`,
`exports::script`, `shell_startup_script`, and the credential-masking gate in
`tools/runtimes/unified_exec.rs`. Niu is grouped with `Sh`/`Cmd`/`PowerShell`
in all of them, matching the fork's existing decision that Niu is not
snapshot-supported.

`wrap_windows_sandbox_exec_request_for_direct_spawn` needed a real merge.
Upstream narrowed helper materialization to the Codex helper only, because
`resolve_exe_for_launch` copies whatever it is given into the helper bin dir.
The fork's read-roots fix is preserved without re-widening that: the workload's
own directory and, when a helper is actually materialized, the helper's
directory are added to `additional_read_roots`.

Every change compiles: `cargo check --all-targets` passes for codex-shell-command,
codex-core, codex-sandboxing, codex-windows-sandbox, codex-tools, codex-apply-patch,
codex-exec-server-protocol, codex-app-server-protocol and codex-cli.

Not yet done on this branch: the fork-owned npm/CI/scripts delta, re-exporting
patches/niu, and refreshing patches/UPSTREAM.
